// Ottava per staff on a grand staff, exercising BOTH directions: the top staff
// runs an 8va (bracket ABOVE its staff, notes drawn an octave lower), the lower
// staff an 8vb (@ottava(bassa) → bracket BELOW its staff, notes drawn an octave
// higher). Each terminates at the loco on ITS OWN staff, and each bracket stacks
// over/under its own staff — the two staves no longer share one score.MusicMarks
// table. The same written pitch shows transposed in measure 1 (8va/8vb) and at
// its true position in measure 2 (loco), while SOUNDING at the written pitch.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/ottava-engraver.cc (per-staff Ottava_spanner_engraver +
// middleCOffset transposition) + lily/axis-group-interface.cc per-staff outside-staff.
octave absolute
title "Multi-staff ottava"
part top { clef treble }
part low { clef bass }
section S {
  top { c'''4@ottava c'''4 c'''4 c'''4 | c'''4@loco c'''4 c'''4 c'''4 | }
  low { c,4@ottava(bassa) c,4 c,4 c,4 | c,4@loco c,4 c,4 c,4 | }
}
structure { S }
score "multi-staff-ottava" { staff top staff low }
